<li about="#cite_note-11" id="cite_note-11" data-mw-footnote-number="11"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwAVY"><a href="#cite_ref-11" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwAVc"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwAVg">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-11" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt51" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" id="mwAVk" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""}}'/><cite id="CITEREFHoskin1996" class="citation book cs1">Hoskin, Keith (1996). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://gwern.net/doc/statistics/decision/1996-hoskin.pdf" class="external text" id="mwAVo">"The 'awful idea of accountability': inscribing people into the measurement of objects."</a> <span class="cs1-format" id="mwAVs">(PDF)</span>. <i id="mwAVw">Accountability: Power, ethos and the technologies of managing</i>. London: International Thomson Business Press. pp.<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAV0"> </span><span class="nowrap" id="mwAV4">265–</span>282.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=bookitem&amp;rft.atitle=The+%E2%80%98awful+idea+of+accountability%E2%80%99%3A+inscribing+people+into+the+measurement+of+objects.&amp;rft.btitle=Accountability%3A+Power%2C+ethos+and+the+technologies+of+managing&amp;rft.place=London&amp;rft.pages=265-282&amp;rft.pub=International+Thomson+Business+Press&amp;rft.date=1996&amp;rft.aulast=Hoskin&amp;rft.aufirst=Keith&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fgwern.net%2Fdoc%2Fstatistics%2Fdecision%2F1996-hoskin.pdf&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AGoodhart%27s+law" class="Z3988" id="mwAV8"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-h-frac-12" id="cite_note-h-frac-12" data-mw-footnote-number="12"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwAWA"><a href="#cite_ref-h-frac_12-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwAWE"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwAWI">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-h-frac-12" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt62" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwAWM" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite journal ","href":"./Template:Cite_journal"},"params":{"last1":{"wt":"Koltun"},"first1":{"wt":"V"},"last2":{"wt":"Hafner"},"first2":{"wt":"D"},"title":{"wt":"The h-index is no longer an effective correlate of scientific reputation."},"journal":{"wt":"PLOS ONE"},"date":{"wt":"2021"},"volume":{"wt":"16"},"issue":{"wt":"6"},"article-number":{"wt":"e0253397"},"doi":{"wt":"10.1371/journal.pone.0253397"},"pmid":{"wt":"34181681"},"pmc":{"wt":"8238192"},"arxiv":{"wt":"2102.03234"},"bibcode":{"wt":"2021PLoSO..1653397K"},"quote":{"wt":"Our results suggest that the use of the h-index in ranking scientists should be reconsidered, and that fractional allocation measures such as h-frac provide more robust alternatives."},"doi-access":{"wt":"free"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFKoltunHafner2021" class="citation journal cs1" about="#mwt62">Koltun, V; Hafner, D (2021). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8238192" class="external text" id="mwAWQ">"The h-index is no longer an effective correlate of scientific reputation"</a>. <i id="mwAWU">PLOS ONE</i>. <b id="mwAWY">16</b> (6) e0253397. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ArXiv_(identifier)" title="ArXiv (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAWc">arXiv</a>:<span class="id-lock-free" title="Freely accessible" id="mwAWg"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2102.03234" class="external text" id="mwAWk">2102.03234</a></span>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bibcode_(identifier)" title="Bibcode (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAWo">Bibcode</a>:<a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2021PLoSO..1653397K" class="external text" id="mwAWs">2021PLoSO..1653397K</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)" title="Doi (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAWw">doi</a>:<span class="id-lock-free" title="Freely accessible" id="mwAW0"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://doi.org/10.1371%2Fjournal.pone.0253397" class="external text" id="mwAW4">10.1371/journal.pone.0253397</a></span>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PMC_(identifier)" title="PMC (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAW8">PMC</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAXA"> </span><span class="id-lock-free" title="Freely accessible" id="mwAXE"><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8238192" class="external text" id="mwAXI">8238192</a></span>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PMID_(identifier)" title="PMID (identifier)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAXM">PMID</a><span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAXQ"> </span><a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34181681" class="external text" id="mwAXU">34181681</a>. <q id="mwAXY">Our results suggest that the use of the h-index in ranking scientists should be reconsidered, and that fractional allocation measures such as h-frac provide more robust alternatives.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=PLOS+ONE&amp;rft.atitle=The+h-index+is+no+longer+an+effective+correlate+of+scientific+reputation.&amp;rft.volume=16&amp;rft.issue=6&amp;rft.artnum=e0253397&amp;rft.date=2021&amp;rft_id=https%3A%